@startuml
title GET /api/ai-agents-teams/bindings/by-channel/{channel} — the channel's public binding set
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Operator / UI" as Caller #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.bindingsByChannel(channel)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "Observer\n(exploratory read)" as Obs #FFF1CC
participant "F1R3Mail bridge\n(the primary consumer)" as Bridge #F7D9E3

Caller -> SDK : bindingsByChannel("mail" | "chat")
SDK -> API : GET .../bindings/by-channel/{channel}
API -> Domain : list bindings
Domain -> Obs : render listChannelBindings(channel);\nexploratory deploy (costs nothing,\nfinalizes nothing)
Obs -> Obs : filterEntriesByField over the public\nbindings map: channel == requested
Obs --> Domain : [binding records]
Domain --> API : [ChannelBinding] — active and inactive,\nflagged; no key material anywhere
API --> SDK : 200 [ChannelBinding]
SDK --> Caller : binding table

Bridge -> Obs : the SAME clause, read directly from the\nobserver on its refresh loop — the HTTP\nmirror never sits in the mail consume path
note right of Bridge #FFF0C7
Chain-read-first: the bridge's TeamDirectory
(RCPT-time accept/450/550) is fed by observer
reads of this binding set, replaced wholesale
each refresh so deactivated bindings never
resurrect.
end note
@enduml
